      "summary": "build_01: Root CMake project for the Argmax custom operator, bounded to the Ascend910B3 (ascend910b/arch22) target with generation-selection plumbing and conditional host/kernel/graph subdirectories.; build_02: Draft build_02: complete isolated build.sh for the float32 Argmax registry-invoke operator; builds only, never installs or activates the package.; build_03: Argmax host CMake build for Ascend910B3 arch22, including host definition, infershape, tiling, ACLNN/L0 op_api, optional l0op opapi linkage, and graph proto packaging.; build_04: Added the op_kernel CMake wiring for the Argmax Ascend910B3 arch22 kernel and package integration.; host_01: Added the Argmax host operator definition with float32 input, int64 output, required axis attribute, and Ascend910B3 AICore registration.; host_02: Added Argmax host shape inference with axis normalization, scalar flattening, and bounded error handling.; host_03: Added Argmax arch22 host tiling for float32 input and int64 output with last-axis reduction, shape/dtype checks, platform-derived row partitioning, UB column tiling, and tiling registration.; kernel_01: Added the arch22 Argmax kernel entry with bounded float32 rank-2/axis-1 support, first-occurrence and NaN-preserving scan semantics, and Init/CopyIn/Compute/CopyOut structure.; kernel_02: Emitted arch22 Argmax kernel class header with numpy-compatible tie/NaN semantics over the (outer, reduceLen, inner) axis decomposition and Init/CopyIn/Compute/CopyOut structure.; kernel_03: Added the authoritative ArgmaxTilingData schema shared by arch22 host tiling and kernel.; kernel_04: Added the arch22 Argmax tiling-key header declaring the float32 input datatype and buffer-mode template parameters used by host tiling and the kernel entry.; api_01: Added the complete public ACLNN L2 header for Argmax with one input, axis attribute, int64 output, and two-stage execute declarations.; api_02: Complete argmax ACLNN L2 implementation for the observed float32 rank-2, axis=1 → int64 profile with explicit validation, L0 dispatch, ViewCopy, and execution synchronization.; api_03: Declared the Argmax L0 ACLNN interface (input, axis, executor) for the float32-to-int64 registry-invoke operator.; api_04: Implemented the Argmax L0 ACLNN API with float32 input validation, axis normalization, int64 output inference, and Ascend kernel launch.; test_adapter_01: Added guarded NumPy-oracle and public asnumpy.argmax tests for the observed float32 axis=1 profile.; test_adapter_02: Generated the unverified Argmax adapter test contract for float32 input and int64 index output.",
